msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:461
msgid "In the left sidebar, select your Business Portfolio, then click on \"Data Sources\" (Sources de données) and choose your Pixel or Dataset."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:462
msgid "Click on the \"Settings\" (Paramètres) tab in the top horizontal menu."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:464
msgid "Locate the \"Dataset ID\" or \"Pixel ID\" section (a 15-16 digit numeric ID, e.g. 123456789012345). Click on it to copy it to your clipboard."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to plugin configuration tab
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:470
#, php-format
msgid "Come back to this page, click on the %s tab above, paste the number into the \"Meta Pixel ID\" field, and click Save Changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:482
msgid "Generate your Conversions API (CAPI) Access Token"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:485
msgid "In Meta Events Manager, stay on the \"Settings\" (Paramètres) tab and scroll down to the \"Conversions API\" section."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:487
msgid "Under \"Set up manually\" (Configurer manuellement), click the blue link \"Generate access token\" (Générer un jeton d'accès)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:489
msgid "Note on System User Token:"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to Meta Business Settings
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:493
#, php-format
msgid "If the \"Generate access token\" link is disabled or grayed out, navigate to %s, create or select an Admin System User, assign your Pixel asset with \"Manage Pixel\" permission, and generate a token with the \"ads_management\" permission."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:494
msgid "Meta Business Settings > System Users"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:499
msgid "Click on the generated token string to copy it (it is a long text beginning with \"EAA...\")."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to plugin configuration tab
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:504
#, php-format
msgid "Paste this token into the \"Conversions API Access Token\" field in the %s tab, and click Save Changes."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:516
msgid "Configure GDPR Consent & Trigger Statuses"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:520
msgid "Enable Browser Pixel:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:521
msgid "Ensure this checkbox is checked. This enables client-side tracking for PageView, ViewContent (product page), AddToCart (AJAX), InitiateCheckout, and client-side Purchase."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:524
msgid "Concord Cookie Banner integration:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:525
msgid "Check \"Require marketing consent from Concord Cookie Banner\". The default cookie prefix is \"concord\". The plugin automatically listens to Concord consent acceptance in real-time without requiring a page refresh!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:528
msgid "Action when consent is refused:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:529
msgid "The default and recommended choice is \"Send anonymized request\". If an customer refuses marketing cookies, CAPI still transmits the order total, currency, purchased item IDs, and deduplication eventID, but strips all customer PII (email, phone, name, address), strips advertising cookies (_fbp, _fbc), and removes IP address / User Agent."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:532
msgid "Trigger statuses:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:533
msgid "By default, \"Processing\" (En cours) and \"Completed\" (Terminée) are enabled. The background Action Scheduler queues the CAPI event as soon as the order transitions into either of these statuses with 100% anti-duplicate safety."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:542
msgid "Test the Connection in Real-Time (Test Event Code)"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to Meta Events Manager
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:549
#, php-format
msgid "In %s, click on the \"Test events\" (Tester les événements) tab."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:554
msgid "In the section \"Confirm your server events are set up correctly\" (Confirmer que les événements de votre serveur sont configurés correctement), copy the test code (e.g. TEST12345)."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to Configuration tab
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:559
#, php-format
msgid "Paste this code into the \"Test Event Code\" field in the %s tab and click Save Changes."
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to Diagnostics tab
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:568
#, php-format
msgid "Go to the %s tab and click the blue button \"Test API Connection (CAPI v21.0)\"."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:573
msgid "Switch to your Meta Events Manager screen: you will see a test \"Purchase\" event appear in green within 2 seconds!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:576
msgid "Crucial Step before going live:"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:577
msgid "Once you have confirmed the test event works, return to the Configuration tab, delete the Test Event Code, and click Save Changes. Leaving the test code in place would mark real production orders as test events in Meta!"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:587
msgid "Verify Front-End Tracking & 100% Deduplication"
msgstr ""

#. translators: %s: HTML link to Chrome Web Store Meta Pixel Helper
#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:594
#, php-format
msgid "Install the official %s extension in Google Chrome."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:595
msgid "Meta Pixel Helper"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:599
msgid "Open your store in an incognito window with a test click parameter in the URL: yourstore.com/?fbclid=TEST_SOYOO_CLICK_123"
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:600
msgid "Accept marketing cookies on your cookie banner: Pixel Helper will immediately detect the Pixel initialization and fire PageView without requiring a reload."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:601
msgid "Visit a product: ViewContent fires. Add to cart: AddToCart fires. Proceed to checkout: InitiateCheckout fires."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:603
msgid "Complete a test order. On the Order Received (Thank You) page, Pixel Helper will display the Purchase event with an eventID parameter (e.g. order_1234)."
msgstr ""

#: includes/class-wfbt-admin-settings.php:606
msgid "In Meta Events Manager, check your events: Meta receives both the Browser event (Pixel) and the Server event (CAPI) sharing the exact same eventID (\"order_1234\") and automatically merges them into a single deduplicated conversion with a green status icon."
msgstr ""

